// ============================================================
// FieldValue - sentinels + explicit-typed value constructors
// ============================================================
// Every function below mints a packed Firestore helper handle surfaced as a
// GML real. This is intentional: packed Firebase handles use only 50 bits, so
// the value is exactly representable as double and can be embedded directly in
// gmval structs/arrays. No real() cast is required. Dynamic GMValue containers
// do not expose a nested int64 wire kind. Feed these values into *_set(),
// *_set_merge(), *_set_merge_fields(), *_update(), *_add(), etc. GML has no
// native way to tag a raw real as a Firestore Timestamp/GeoPoint/Reference/Blob/
// integer/sentinel, so these constructors provide that exact typing.

